- [observed + will_said] HOLO-PHEXT BENCH512: BOARDY'S BAR NOT MET (measured 2026-11-16, task 31.8.10/10.9.14/8.7.9): at a 512 MB base, commit latency is not O(delta) - libphext::append re-tokenizes the whole in-memory WAL per batch, so median commit latency saws ~8.5 ms to ~85 ms as the WAL grows 0 to 8.9 MB between folds; checkpoint/fold is O(base) at ~1.4-1.7 s, and commits caught in a fold see p50 1,369 ms. Correctness held (the base still parses as plain phext after checkpoint; kill -9 recovery exact). Scoped fix: true suffix append in libphext + structural-sharing overlay, with the fold off the writer's path or incremental. Will directed that the next libphext release, v0.6.3, be scheduled to include these performance optimizations.

