- [will_said + observed] WILLBOT REV9-REV13 - SPACING ITERATIONS (Will, 2026-11-16 evening): Will's standard - much less spacing between characters and much more between words (space advance 250 -> 420 from rev9). Rev9: advances x0.88, kern target 40 - Will: letter spacing still double what he uses. Rev10 (23:24 CST): advances x0.80, kern target 20. Rev12 discarded the template boxes entirely (advance = 0.75 x ink width, mean advance 581 -> 378). Rev13 (~23:50 CST, Will: eliminate the extra whitespace, letters nearly edge to edge): every glyph's ink shifted to bounding-box 0, advance = ink width exactly, collision-only kern at 6-unit clearance (80 pairs). Each revision deployed and hash-verified live on quickfork.net and singularitywatch.org; rev13 WOFF2 SHA-256 c297c771... [will_said] Origin recalled 23:40-23:41 CST: something about the original font boxes was not designed for his handwriting; he fought the MyScriptFont template boxes in 2015 and gave up when it lost his interest - why the font sat untouched ~11 years.

- [will_said + observed] WILLBOT REV14 + WILLBOTMONO V1.1 (Will, 2026-11-16 23:56 CST): Will directed kerning like normal computer text - very tightly packed letters - for both Willbot and WillbotMono. Rev14: LSB=RSB=25 (advance = ink + 50) plus expanded optical kern, all 7,225 ordered pairs over an 85-character set kerned to a uniform 35-unit outline distance; deployed and hash-verified live on both sites (WOFF2 SHA-256 2f63fbcb...). WillbotMono v1.1 supersedes the 450-unit-cell build: fixed 520-unit cell, ink centered, space = cell, no kern table, isFixedPitch set (WOFF2 SHA-256 045780a5...); not wired into the websites.
